1.17
log
@Increase yellow high alarm limit for window infrared temp by 1C from 90 to 91C.
Per Jim Sebek:
The cavity D window is known to operate at a higher temperature than that of the
other cavities.  The window temperature depends on both the electric field at
the window and the window coating.  The cavity D window was replaced at the same
time that the Cavity C window was replaced at the end of the 2011 run.  The
procedure for the coating of the new windows had changed, changing the
conductivity and increasing the temperature.  The temperatures rise to this
level each time there is a low alpha run as can be seem from the history buffers
from last year.  These elevated temperatures are still below the values of
150degC to which the windows were tested.  If we continue low alpha runs, we
should change the warning limits of the PVs.
@
text
@d52 1
a52 1
          {$(RRRS),KLYS,:VACM      ,""  ,SUMY,"Ion Pump Current",  10,  15,  5 , -10, -15, -10, 100,-100,uA      ,3,0.01,0.001,5,18, 28,29,12,27,12,13 }
@


